WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.643
Peter arrived at the shore of Kidd’s Creek where the Jolly Roger was anchored.

2
00:00:05.644 --> 00:00:08.900
He had quickly crawled across the island.

3
00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:14.360
After seeing the silent crocodile, Peter had decided to imitate it.

4
00:00:14.361 --> 00:00:22.759
In fact, he tick-tocked so perfectly the way the creature had done that the other animals let him pass unharmed.

5
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:30.935
The crocodile, which had become fond of the sound, followed him, hoping to get his tick-tock back.

6
00:00:30.936 --> 00:00:38.157
"This time, it’s Hook or me!" Peter vowed to himself, then dived into the water.

7
00:00:38.158 --> 00:00:43.635
He had been tick-tocking so long that he hardly thought about it anymore.

8
00:00:43.636 --> 00:00:50.346
He swam to the ship and climbed up the side—tick-tocking all the while.

9
00:00:50.347 --> 00:00:54.896
When the boys looked over the side, he signaled them to be quiet.

10
00:00:54.897 --> 00:00:58.881
Then he climbed around the hull to the other side of the ship.

11
00:00:58.882 --> 00:01:05.151
He peeked over the rail and saw the boys in chains and Wendy tied to the mast.

12
00:01:05.152 --> 00:01:10.154
They all saw him too, and he gave them another signal to be quiet.

13
00:01:10.155 --> 00:01:13.581
Hook was trembling on the deck.

14
00:01:13.582 --> 00:01:18.151
"How clever of me!" Peter thought, grinning.

15
00:01:18.152 --> 00:01:23.251
At the back of the deck was the cabin. Peter watched the cabin door.

16
00:01:23.252 --> 00:01:27.641
When one of the pirates came out, Peter stabbed him with his dagger.

17
00:01:27.642 --> 00:01:32.310
He covered the pirate’s mouth to muffle his dying moan.

18
00:01:32.311 --> 00:01:36.307
The boys watched as Peter threw the pirate overboard.

19
00:01:36.308 --> 00:01:40.329
There was a loud splash, followed by silence.

20
00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:43.925
Then Peter vanished into the cabin.

21
00:01:43.926 --> 00:01:47.770
"Pirate number one!" whispered Slightly.

22
00:01:47.771 --> 00:01:52.815
The pirates had heard a big splash, and then the tick-tocking had stopped.

23
00:01:52.816 --> 00:01:57.313
All they could hear now was the sound of their breathing.

24
00:01:57.314 --> 00:02:04.680
"It’s gone, Captain," Smee said, wiping his spectacles. "All is still again."

25
00:02:04.681 --> 00:02:08.437
Listening hard, Hook slowly raised his head.

26
00:02:08.438 --> 00:02:17.543
Hearing nothing, he got up and yelled, "Get those boys on the plank!" His nerve was back.

27
00:02:17.544 --> 00:02:22.718
But the boys had seen him act like a coward, and it made him hate them more.

28
00:02:22.719 --> 00:02:27.387
"Fetch my whip from the cabin!" he yelled to one of his pirates.

29
00:02:27.388 --> 00:02:34.587
"The cabin! Peter’s in there!" thought the children, as they looked at each other.

30
00:02:34.588 --> 00:02:40.348
"Ay, ay," said Bill Jukes, cheerfully opening the cabin door.

31
00:02:40.349 --> 00:02:45.713
As soon as the door closed behind him, a terrible scream was heard from inside.

32
00:02:45.714 --> 00:02:49.535
It was followed by a sound like a rooster crowing.

33
00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:54.045
The boys knew the sound, but the pirates looked puzzled.

34
00:02:54.046 --> 00:02:58.918
"Number two!" Slightly said quietly to the boys.

35
00:02:58.919 --> 00:03:02.118
"What was that?" shouted Hook.

36
00:03:02.119 --> 00:03:10.998
Cecco thought for a moment, and then ran into the cabin. Shocked, he stumbled out.

37
00:03:10.999 --> 00:03:14.505
"What’s the matter?" Hook yelled.

38
00:03:14.506 --> 00:03:18.306
"Juke’s been stabbed to death," cried Cecco.

39
00:03:18.307 --> 00:03:23.881
"The cabin is dark, and there is some terrible thing in there. It’s . . . crowing."

40
00:03:23.882 --> 00:03:29.699
"Cecco," Hook ordered, "go find out what that thing is!"

41
00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:35.965
"No, no! I can’t do that!" Cecco said, desperately.

42
00:03:35.966 --> 00:03:42.729
Hook lifted his iron claw. "Are you disobeying me?" he yelled.

43
00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:48.078
Trembling, Cecco followed Hook’s order and went slowly into the cabin.

44
00:03:48.079 --> 00:03:54.217
Again, they all heard a deadly scream followed by a crowing sound.

45
00:03:54.218 --> 00:03:57.625
"Number three!" Slightly called out.

46
00:03:57.626 --> 00:04:02.147
Hook yelled at his crew. "Who will get this crowing thing?"

47
00:04:02.148 --> 00:04:07.041
"Wait until Cecco comes out," cried Starkey.

48
00:04:07.042 --> 00:04:12.576
The other pirates agreed. "Yes, let’s wait!"

49
00:04:12.577 --> 00:04:17.403
"Did I hear you volunteer, Starkey?" said Hook.

50
00:04:17.404 --> 00:04:24.799
"No, by thunder!" growled Starkey. "I’ll hang before I go in there."

51
00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:29.960
"Is this mutiny?" asked Hook, lifting his claw.

52
00:04:29.961 --> 00:04:36.958
"Captain, please, have mercy!" the fearful pirate begged.

53
00:04:36.959 --> 00:04:43.325
Starkey backed away, and Hook strode toward him, his hook ready to strike.

54
00:04:43.326 --> 00:04:49.146
Starkey looked around for help, but all the other pirates were looking down at their feet.

55
00:04:49.147 --> 00:04:54.958
With a hopeless scream, Starkey leapt off the ship and into the sea.

56
00:04:54.959 --> 00:05:03.130
"Number four!" called Slightly, happily.

